1. Restructured the mock session to exactly match what the component expects
2. Added more required user properties (locale, teams, organizationId)
3. Made sure the session structure is consistent whether authenticated or not
4. Added a wrapper div with full width to ensure proper rendering
5. Properly handled the case when mockSession is false
6. Ensured all required properties for the user object are present
7. Made sure the session status is properly set for both authenticated and unauthenticated states

The key changes here are:
- Providing a complete user object with all required properties
- Ensuring the session structure matches exactly what the component expects
- Proper handling of the authentication state

This should resolve the "Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'role')" error because we're now providing a properly structured session object with all required properties.

